      "display_username": "Rabit",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Personally, I&#39;m okay with delays in GSF if it helps ensure we have a better game - that has to be the priority, as I&#39;d want their second game venture to be at least as successful as their first. Also, since they included Vengeance in the last Kickstarter, they now have some pressure on that to get it out in a timely fashion, whereas GSF has no such pressures (other than anticipation!  :wink: ).\n\nAs much as I&#39;d love to get Vengeance at GenCon, it&#39;s not something I want, as they would not have enough time to fully play test it at this point.\n\nAnd &gt;G is fully-loaded working on their current projects. I&#39;d rather have them improve the company and the work they&#39;re currently doing than put out comics.\n\nJust me, though.  :sunglasses: ",
